After the 2026 "template-only no-match silently throws" fix
(resolve: silently discard template-only no-match per [temp.deduct]/8),
the surface symptom changed: the libc++ std::tuple constructor
overload set (which involves many SFINAE-guarded forwarding-reference
templates) no longer emits CONVERSION ERROR when deduction fails.
Instead, the enclosing convert_function catches the silent throw and
discards main()'s body, so the __CPROVER_assert calls never make it
into the goto program and verification "succeeds" vacuously.
Expected-when-fixed now requires main's assertion to be SUCCESS in
the output; until libc++ tuple deduction actually completes through
CBMC's front-end, this test stays on the KNOWNBUG list.
Minimal header-free reproducer: cpp11_tuple_leaf_no_body.
Round-10 update: the non-type base-pack root is FIXED
(cpp11_nontype_base_pack CORE); the library test now surfaces a
VISIBLE next layer (tuple_element/get resolution: "found no match for
symbol 'get'") instead of silent wrong-code.  Re-reduce next.
Round-11 third batch (2026-08-04): the get redirect now compares
parameter TYPES position-normalized ([dcl.fct]/5, [temp.over.link]/6);
the whole family RUNS BMC end-to-end.  Remaining layer visible as
no-body FAILUREs: std::__1::get<0,...>'s DEFINITION body is not
instantiated for the call (apply_basic reaches VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL
but main is still dropped -- props=0, caught by this desc).
